X11 WSI: without TAWC-DRI, present through standard DRI3 and Present.

Termux:X11 has no TAWC-DRI, but imports an Android hardware buffer read from a socket passed as a DRI3 buffer fd
(modifier 1255). Each swapchain buffer is imported once as a pixmap, frames are PresentPixmap requests, and
PresentIdleNotify releases buffers the way TAWC-DRI's buffer-release event does. Its depth-24 windows show any
buffer opaque, so their swapchains can be OPAQUE whatever the format (Zink always asks for it).

Also accept DirectColor visuals, as Mesa's X11 WSI does: GLX gives Zink's windows one, and its pixels are laid out
like TrueColor's.

